  ## Security Layers (Defense in Depth)

  | Layer | Tool | Purpose |
  |---|---|---|
  | 1 — Perimeter | Hetzner Firewall | Block everything except xxxx |
  | 2 — Host | UFW | OS-level firewall rules |
  | 3 — Intrusion prevention | Fail2Ban | Auto-ban IPs after failed SSH attempts |
  | 4 — Threat intelligence | CrowdSec | Community-sourced IP blocklist |
  | 5 — Private network | Tailscale | Zero Trust access for management |
  | 6 — Authentication | SSH keys | No password auth — keys only |
  | 7 — Isolation | Docker networks | Services can't reach each other unless explicitly allowed |
  | 8 — Vulnerability scanning | Trivy | CVE scanning on Docker images |

  **Zero Trust principle:** No implicit trust based on network location. Every access request is authenticated and authorized explicitly.

