  ## Cost Comparison: Self-hosted vs AWS equivalent

  | Service | Self-hosted (Hetzner) | AWS equivalent | AWS monthly cost |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | VM (2 vCPU, 4GB) | Included | EC2 t3.medium | ~AUD 45 |
  | Database | Included | RDS PostgreSQL t3.micro | ~AUD 25 |
  | Load balancer | Nginx (free) | ALB | ~AUD 25 |
  | Monitoring | Uptime Kuma (free) | CloudWatch | ~AUD 10 |
  | **Total** | **~AUD 7/month** | | **~AUD 105/month** |

  **Insight for sales:** A startup choosing self-hosted IaaS vs managed PaaS (AWS) saves ~93% on infrastructure costs but takes on operational overhead — security patching, monitoring, backups. The
  value proposition of AWS is **operational simplicity and managed reliability**, not raw compute cost.

